\name{effmap.remove.all}
\alias{effmap.remove.all}
\title{Removes all stored effect maps}

\description{
Removes all stored effect maps.
}

\usage{
effmap.remove.all()
}
\value{
An invisible \code{list} returned by the compiled routine. The list is an implementation-level result containing the arguments returned by the compiled routine; the function is primarily called for its side effect of removing all effect maps.
}
